Thank you very much! It works as supposed.

Finally, I wrote a nimble function for convolution.
nimConvolution = nimbleFunction(
    run = function(a = double(1), b = double(1)) {
        L <- dim(a)[1]
        ans <- inprod(a[L+1-1:L],b)
        return(ans)
        returnType(double(0))
    }
)

However, it worked for that function, but if I would write directly in the code such as:
    for (k in 52:(K-1)) {
        conv[k+1] <- inprod(exposure[k+1-1:k],incubationPeriod[1:k])
#         conv[k+1] <- nimConvolution(exposure[1:k],incubationPeriod[1:k]) - top line instead of this line
        observed[k+1] ~ dpois(conv[k+1])
    }
it would throw me an error:
Error: Error processing model: something is wrong with the index k_plus_1 - 1:k.

